-- title:
--   Regular special fibre from unramifiedness in codimension one
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$ admitting a ring embedding $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange` of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$, and let $j \in K$, $j \ne 0$, have Laurent expansion the coefficient image of the $j$-expansion `jq`. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$. Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` (the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ to that of $A[j^{-1}]$), and $\varpi_z$ the image of $\varpi$ in the stalk at $z$ under $\Gamma\mathrm{Spec}$, the structural morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ on global sections and the germ map; assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk. Assume $z$ is the image of a point $y$ of the $j$-finite chart $\mathrm{Spec}(A_{\mathrm{fin}})$, $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, with $y$ corresponding to a maximal ideal, that there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi : A_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \Omega$ into an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel exactly $y$, that $\varphi(j) \notin$ `ssJSet q Ω` (so some elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has a nonzero point killed by $q$), and that every $b \in A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ which is a non-unit of $W_0$ lies in $y$. Let $K_0 \le K$ be the `laurentBaseChange` of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, with $j_0 \in K_0$, $j_0 \ne 0$, again expanding to the coefficient image of `jq`, let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the floor chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀` to $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ compatible with the inclusion $K_0 \hookrightarrow K$, and assume the floor model is smooth over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Then, regarding $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ as an algebra over the floor chart algebra via $\iota$: if $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is unramified over the floor chart algebra at every prime $\mathfrak Q \subseteq y$ of height $1$, the quotient of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak X, z}$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is purity of the branch locus (Zariski–Nagata, in the form of Auslander–Buchsbaum) applied to the finite normal cover of the smooth $\Gamma_0(M')$-floor model by the normalised full-level model: unramifiedness in codimension one over a regular two-dimensional base forces regularity of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the stalk at the given closed point. It feeds the regularity statement for the special fibre at maximal, non-supersingular points specialising to the centre of the Gauss valuation.
